**Allegro ETRM — Contract #PPA-2021-012**
Counterparty: High Plains Wind LLC | Product: Wind (120 MW nameplate) | COD: March 1, 2022 | Base Price: $24.00/MWh | Escalator: '2.0% or CPI, whichever is greater, applied annually on COD anniversary' | Term: 25 yr.

**SharePoint — /Renewables/PPAs/HighPlainsWind/Contract_Amendments/**
No amendments on file. Original executed PPA only.

**SharePoint — /Renewables/PPAs/HighPlainsWind/Invoicing/**
File: 'HP_Wind_Escalator_Calc_2023.xlsx' (uploaded Mar 2023 by r.okafor)
Worksheet shows: 2023 price = $24.00 x 1.028 = $24.67/MWh
Cell B4 note: 'Used CPI-U All Items, national avg, per Sarah's guidance'
File: 'HP_Wind_Escalator_Calc_2024.xlsx' (uploaded Mar 2024 by r.okafor)
Worksheet shows: 2024 price = $24.67 x 1.032 = $25.46/MWh
Cell B4 note: 'CPI-U All Items again. Developer didn't dispute.'

**Outlook — From: billing@highplainswind.com (Feb 18, 2026)**
To: sarah.lindqvist@conduitenergy.com, ap-renewables@conduitenergy.com
Subject: Year 4 Price Adjustment — PPA-2021-012

'Per Section 7.3(b), please find attached our Year 4 escalator calculation. We are applying CPI-W (Wage Earners) for the Denver-Aurora-Lakewood MSA which was 4.1% for the applicable period, resulting in a new price of $26.50/MWh. The contract does not specify which CPI variant or geography; CPI-W regional is the most appropriate index for energy infrastructure in our operating region.'

**Teams — #renewable-contracts (Feb 19, 2026, 11:15 AM)**
@sarah.lindqvist: Heads up — High Plains is trying to switch CPI indices on us. They want CPI-W Denver metro (4.1%) instead of the CPI-U national (2.8%) we've used the last two years.
@dave.morton: Can they do that? Contract just says 'CPI' right?
@sarah.lindqvist: Yeah, it's ambiguous. Section 7.3(b) literally just says 'CPI.'
@rachel.okafor: I set precedent in Year 1 using CPI-U national because that's what our other PPAs use. They didn't object then.
@dave.morton: Did we get that confirmed in writing from them?
@rachel.okafor: Not explicitly. They just paid/accepted the invoice at our calculated rate.
@sarah.lindqvist: Right. Two years of acquiescence isn't nothing but it's not a signed amendment either.
@dave.morton: Loop legal? This is a $180K/yr delta at their volumes.
@sarah.lindqvist: Already did. Amy said she'd look at it Thursday.
[Emoji reaction from @amy.vasquez: eyes emoji]

**SAP — PO History for Vendor #400156 (High Plains Wind LLC)**
PO Year 2023: Unit price $24.67/MWh — matched to invoice, paid.
PO Year 2024: Unit price $25.46/MWh — matched to invoice, paid.
No disputed line items on record.
